  |\nL159: cite78†README.md | cite78†README.md |    |\nL160: ## Repository files navigation\nL161: \nL162:   *   * cite79†README L163:   * cite79†MIT license L164: \nL165: More items\nL166: \nL167: # FREESH: Fair, Resource- and Energy-Efficient Scheduling for LLM Serving on Heterogeneous GPUs\nL168: \nL169: > A modular routing + scheduling system for LLM inference that jointly optimizes energy/carbon, SLOs, and fairness across heterogeneous, geo-distributed GPU clusters.\nL170: ## Highlights\nL171:   * Three-layer co-design\nL172:     * Pool-level (slow timescale): MILP-based optimizer for cross-region placement, request partitioning, and tensor-parallel (TP) mode selection with switchable energy or carbon objectives.\nL173:     * GPU-level (seconds): MIAD (Multiplicative Increase, Additive Decrease) dynamic frequency control to reduce power while meeting SLOs.\nL174:     * Request-level (sub-second): LLF (Least Laxity First) preemptive scheduler for fairness and lower tail latency (reduces FCFS head-of-line blocking).\nL175:   * Six “control knobs”: site selection, partitioning, request type, execution mode (TP / model-GPU pairing), frequency (DVFS/MIAD), and scheduling policy (LLF).\nL176:   * Carbon-intensity aware routing: leverages spatiotemporal grid carbon signals to shift work to cleaner regions/periods.\nL177:   * Plug-and-play: integrates with common inference runtimes (e.g., vLLM) and multiple solvers (e.g., Gurobi / open-source backends).\nL178: > Full method and evaluations: cite80†https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.00807†arxiv.org L179: ## Cold-switch experiment\nL180: \nL181: See cite81†Cold_Switch for a runnable cold TP-switch experiment with online, replaceable output-length prediction, Monitor and MIAD. This experiment does not implement LLF; it is separate from the LLF simulation and pool optimizer.\nL182: \nL183: ## About\nL184: \nL185: No description, website, or topics provided.\nL186: \nL187: ### Resources\nL188: \nL189: cite82†Readme L190: \nL191: cite83†MIT license L192: \nL193: cite84†Activity L194: \nL195: ### Stars\nL196: \nL197: 9 stars\nL198: \nL199: ### Watchers\nL200: \nL201: 0 watching\nL202: \nL203: ### Forks\nL204: \nL205: cite85†0 forks L206: \nL207: cite86†Report repository L208: \nL209: ## Releases\nL210: \nL211: ## Packages\nL212: ## Contributors\nL213: \nL214: ## Languages\nL215: \nL216: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n"